# Client environment (Vite).
#
# The frontend needs NOTHING to run in the default setup: it calls the API at
# the relative path `/api`, which Vite proxies in dev and nginx proxies in the
# Docker/production build. So for a same-origin deploy you can skip this file
# entirely.
#
# Only Vite vars prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser, and they are
# baked in at BUILD time (`npm run build` / the Docker image build) — not read
# at runtime. Never put secrets here; anything in here ships to every visitor.

# --- optional -------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute API base URL. Set ONLY if the client and API are served from
# different origins (e.g. client on https://signoff.app, API on
# https://api.signoff.app). Include the /api suffix. When you set this, also
# set CLIENT_ORIGIN on the server so CORS + the session cookie work.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.signoff.app/api
